detailed way for example it's almost

107
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,200
always better to show hotpots of crime

108
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:13,879
using a density map rather than a chop

109
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:16,639
plma but sometimes we have little choice

110
00:04:16,639 --> 00:04:18,840
but to use a corpath map because data is

111
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:21,199
only available for areas not in

112
00:04:21,199 --> 00:04:22,479
individual

113
00:04:22,479 --> 00:04:25,960
locations so in summary lots of useful

114
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:28,720
data is published for areas rather than

115
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,680
individual streets or

116
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,440
addresses governments typically publish

117
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,720
data for both administrative and

118
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:38,320
statistical areas and whenever we use a

119
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,800
corop map we need to consider the

